rlier today we sent Neutron’s Stage 2 and Thrust Module out of the Neutron Factory and onto a barge for transport through Chesapeake Bay to Wallops Island in Virginia. Once it arrives, the Thrust Module will go straight onto the launch mount at LC-3 for check outs and the beginning of wider systems demonstrations including integrated fluids tests and module-to-launch-mount interface checkouts. With no strongback on the launch mount by design, Neutron’s Thrust Module is the rocket’s only physical interface to the launch pad, which this upcoming test campaign enables us to test early before the entire vehicle comes together.","image":"https://cdn4.telesco.pe/file/ZI7ZLuMcoIWEgYgtpYtUKl7iKdN7YBKq0LCiyVPXyYBvySL3yJAccR4CIJ5-SQq8RMLrXnUfL2UROUnHmqA9oo44ajEBO-7QWE-gbnQI1SJpr0RMKDkARjT9DUIGURF0D1l19XzZe-Zj0R7ijE7z_z0nItpwb7HCUdPAT2I8JSMRUr1Me_yucfhuWpHkEJ_XRXuaPP9h_cu_FVcNk1gQgSxNdzgat1cJAywI4USWKI-T9BZ0NMhpRAvdkWu7RvCYVSA9XFV8Ru_DTOLv9UwQZ4vtZKpcYrzixUj4uoSWfJTZg0onaKSx8LlP04mWMKd7BvnZLqMSlW__2bGcuS2U0g.jpg","video":"","hasVideo":false}]
